WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.350
Different people handle loss differently.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.270
There are sore losers.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.029
There are angry losers.

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:10.210
There are depressive losers.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:15.820
There are narcissists who tend to go more
in the direction of I didn't want to win anyway.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.520
There's a really broad range of reaction to
loss and it often changes over time.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.390
We're seeing something really interesting
on Fox News, which is that suddenly they are

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:31.109
all about their feelings and the feelings
of conservatives and the feelings of Trump.

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:37.140
That's how everybody feels about the election
numbers, how everybody feels about the election

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:42.390
results, how some of their feelings are now
hurt by what has taken place.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:45.170
And you've got to see some of these examples.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:50.360
Here is one from Fox and Friends yesterday
morning where Ainsley Earhardt, one of the

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:56.780
hosts, says, you know, staunch conservatives,
they feel defeated.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.600
They has a sad for lack of a better term.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.920
Take a listen to what I think people who are
staunch conservatives in our country just

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.840
feel so, just so defeated because of this
election.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.180
They do feel like it was rigged.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.770
And then to see what's happening in Georgia
that the Democrats could have the House Democrats

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.440
could have the Senate and the presidency.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.980
And that's that's the danger.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.780
Did you hear that?

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:25.230
It's disheartening for staunch conservatives
that they lost.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:29.130
Where was this understanding back in 2008?

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.430
Where was this understanding back in 2012?

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:33.770
I don't recall it from these same people.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:39.450
Now, part of the irony of all this is that
the right has this idea of the facts don't

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.030
care about your feelings.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:45.159
That's a meme that they love pushing on to
the left.

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:47.280
And now they all need time.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:53.880
And we need to be careful with their feelings
because they are fragile and and and disheartened

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.840
by what they are seeing.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.710
Here's another while, by the way, advocating
for the essentially for the setting aside

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:06.110
of the actual results because they just feel
bad about it.

